      "writtenOn": "2024-12-02T18:27:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In order to reduce the risk of surprises to engineers, I want to adhere to the usual semantics of `fopen()`, `fwrite()`, and `fflush()`, under which it is a no-op to call `fflush()` on a `FILE` opened in non-buffered mode.\n\nI agree that it is probably rare to have a helper method that uses `fprintf()` followed by `fflush()`, and to call that helper variously with files opened in buffered and un-buffered mode, but it could be done, and in such case it is desirable that the `fflush()` is a no-op in case it is unbuffered.",
      "parentUuid": "32a9f5c1_ab694828",
      "revId": "a64040460b852d18f7d339f42d5fd741c6d77c6e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
